  "story": {
    "bet": [
      {
        "text": "Always be on the move: take cargo the moment the robot touches it, on either side, and shoot while moving from many positions.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s8"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "demand": [
      {
        "text": "In qualifications, all ranking points: score 18 or 20 cargo without relying heavily on partners, and climb to the traversal rung while leaving partners room. In playoffs more alliances climb that high, so cargo in the upper hub must make the difference, starting in auto, where points are doubled and there is no defense.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s8"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "auto": [
      {
        "text": "The robot follows precalculated splines with feedforward and feedback. The binder notes that five cargo in auto lowers the alliance's cargo ranking point threshold.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s8"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In the first Einstein final an analyst saw it shoot an opponent cargo to the hangar zone and later score two of three.",
        "basis": "observer",
        "src": [
          "s17"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "cycle": [
      {
        "text": "Either intake feeds the Serializer, which stores the first cargo opposite the active intake and sends wrong-color cargo out through the shooter. The turret tracks the goal. While the driver allows it, the robot shoots when turret, hood and wheel speed are right, mostly from the edge of the tarmac.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s8",
          "s18",
          "s19"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "endgame": [
      {
        "text": "Automated, with manual overrides: the Elevator pulls on the mid rung, the Reaction Arm meets the underside of the truss and levels the robot, and the Stinger hooks the traversal rung. It leaves space for partners; the team counts two triple traversal climbs at one regional.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s8",
          "s18",
          "s19"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "fallback": [
      {
        "text": "The operator can move the turret by hand when the camera tracks a bad target. The playoff slides prepared three scorers in a triangle, or two scorers and a defender; the alliance changed its third robot for the last Einstein final.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s20",
          "s3",
          "s21"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "gave_up": [
      {
        "text": "Swerve, turret and two intakes left the drivers a few afternoons of practice before the first event. At 124.9 lb the team fought weight all season. Feeding and shooting takes several hundred milliseconds, so sudden acceleration could spoil a shot.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s22",
          "s23",
          "s19"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The team says 1678 was far better at crossing the whole field for any ball.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s22"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "changed": [
      {
        "text": "After the reveal: totally different intakes, several climber parts and small shooter tweaks. The original shooter's small Fairlane wheels had given way to a 9 in flywheel. The elevator went from two motors to one to gain weight for a hooded shooter.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s24",
          "s18",
          "s25"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "After its second regional the team added aimed ejection of opponent cargo, and at the championship corrected it for robot velocity.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s26",
          "s27"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "outcome": [
      {
        "text": "50-5-1 in official play; won the Galileo division, won the championship; pick 1 of the Galileo alliance on Einstein; ranked 2 of the pooled top 20 (OPR 68.28, Galileo).",
        "basis": "record",
        "src": [
          "s1",
          "s2"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "functions": [
    {
      "name": "Drivebase",
      "does": [
        "drive",
        "structure"
      ],
      "type": "swerve",
      "serves": [],
      "solves": [
        {
          "text": "Cover the field quickly and avoid defense",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s8"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "SDS MK4i modules with Falcons and L3 reduction; free speed",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s8"
          ],
          "value": 18,
          "unit": "ft/s"
        },
        {
          "text": "Chosen over MK4 for the inverted motors and wider track",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s28"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "2x1x1/16 in aluminum tube frame with a 1/8 in bellypan without pockets and the battery in the middle",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Module setpoints are coordinated, also in teleop, and module flips are decided globally; some scrub was allowed because the drivers preferred it",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s29"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "At boot the code waits for several valid readings from each absolute encoder, which took over 10 seconds",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s30"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Bearings were added to the modules to support the Falcon shafts; the team does not know whether they were necessary or helpful",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s50"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cost": [
        {
          "text": "The solid bellypan was heavy: the writer thinks it should have been pocketed",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s23"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The L3 gears were already in hand; everything else equal, L2 would have been better; another team post says that with so much power a suboptimal ratio matters less than it used to",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s31",
            "s49"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Dual intakes",
      "does": [
        "acquire"
      ],
      "type": "over-bumper roller intakes on both sides",
      "pieces": [
        "cargo"
      ],
      "serves": [
        "hub-upper"
      ],
      "solves": [
        {
          "text": "Grab cargo at any driving speed or angle and shorten retrieval",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s8"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Robot-width rollers on a pneumatic four-bar; one Falcon drives two belt-driven rollers per intake",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Front roller: 3 in polycarbonate tube with anti-slip tape; back roller: 1 in aluminum tube with heat shrink",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s8",
            "s34"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Side plates of 1/4 in polycarbonate, compliant to impacts",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Compression on the cargo judged optimal in prototypes, about",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s16"
          ],
          "value": 1.5,
          "unit": "in"
        },
        {
          "text": "The tape is a non-abrasive 3M anti-slip textured vinyl. Two team posts disagree on grip: one says no more than clean gum rubber, surgical tubing or Fairlane wheels, its gain being light rollers; a later one calls that wrong and says it had the most grip without ball damage",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s32",
            "s33"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The links turn directly on greased anodized aluminum, with short dead axles clamped by a bolt; only the two rollers join the sides",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s34"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The operator deploys and retracts them, with no sensor",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s20"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The championship intake was the fifth version; the deploy geometry was revised after the first regional to be quicker and need less force",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s18",
            "s35"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Serializer",
      "does": [
        "transfer",
        "retain"
      ],
      "type": "two-sided funnel with color sorting",
      "pieces": [
        "cargo"
      ],
      "serves": [
        "hub-upper"
      ],
      "solves": [
        {
          "text": "Bring cargo from two wide intakes into one stream for the shooter without jamming",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s8"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Per side: two 6 in polycarbonate wheels with grip tape and powered 1 in top rollers, on one Falcon through bevel gears",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s8",
            "s36"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Holds a ball on each side and one in the center",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s18"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Surgical tubing gives way to the ball, then pushes it up from below against the feeder rollers, in both directions",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s18",
            "s36"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A stored ball is shuffled across so a second ball, perhaps of the wrong color, can pass to the shooter",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s36"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Three beam breaks count and locate the balls",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s8"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cost": [
        {
          "text": "Square nuts pressed into the printed mounts spun free in the off-season, which made it hard to take the Serializer off",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s36"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
