            "s18"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The Elevator grabs the second rung and pulls; the Reaction Arm hits the underside of the truss and tilts the robot level",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "One Falcon and #25 chain; the binder gives a 41:1 reduction, a team post says 21.5:1 was used at Silicon Valley and the championship",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s8",
            "s25"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Load: the binder says over 500 lb, a team post about 380 lb on the elevator",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s8",
            "s25"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "With a slower ratio the arm met the truss as the robot swung away, which made much higher loads; after the ratio changed, it met the truss on the swing back and momentum helped; the post does not name the ratios",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s40"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Surgical tubing pulls the arm out; printed hooks on the arm stay caught on the hook standoffs until the carriage rises",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s41",
            "s8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A plate on the hooks is pushed against the truss to align the robot",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A team post says the climb, from starting to pull on the mid rung, took just under",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s42"
          ],
          "value": 2,
          "unit": "s"
        },
        {
          "text": "The same post says that once the tail is past the traversal rung, gravity back-drives the elevator and finishes the transfer without power",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s42"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A commenter timed one climb at 4.76 s off the floor and 11.98 s from entering the hangar zone",
          "basis": "observer",
          "src": [
            "s43"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The carriage rolls on bearing blocks with 12 mm bearings, which held through the championship and were replaced in the off-season",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s51"
          ]
        }
      ]
